// A deliberately crowded bed, for measuring what a per-tick breeder lookup
// costs -- not a question about the world, a question about the code.
//
// **The pessimal case for a per-colony breeder index, on purpose.** The
// index it is built to test reads in time proportional to *one colony's*
// breeders; the full-slot scan it replaces reads in time proportional to
// *every organism in the world*. Twenty small colonies would flatter the
// index and say nothing. So this is ONE colony, as large as the bed will
// seat, among as many plants as will grow -- the arrangement where the
// index has the most breeders to walk and the scan has the most organisms.
//
// **Plants are placed at frame 0 alongside the colony, and that ordering is
// the whole reason this file exists rather than a flag on `played_bed`.** A
// grown bed refuses a colony: `found_colony_of` needs bare footing and by
// frame 6,000 the vegetation and its seed litter have the surface, which is
// measured at 8 founders seated of 52 (see the played bed's own note). At
// frame 0 every plant is still a single seed, so the founders seat and the
// canopy closes around them afterwards. That gives both halves at once --
// a large colony AND a large organism count -- which no ordering that
// grows the bed first can produce.
//
// **Fed on a repeating timeline, because the lookup is gated on
// affordability.** The scan runs only for an animal that could already pay
// for a child, so a starving colony never reaches it and would measure
// nothing -- the "rare tick" argument that justified the scan in the first
// place was made on exactly such a bed. Windfall arriving every 1,200
// frames keeps a large fraction of the colony at its breeding bar, which is
// the state the cost is supposed to be measured in.
//
// **What it actually seats, measured rather than asked for: 126 animals of
// the 1,000 requested**, spanning x 5..506 -- the colony saturates the bed
// edge to edge and the count is bounded by the width, not by the number.
// The request is left high on purpose so the bed stays saturated if it is
// ever widened; `found_colony_of` seats what fits and reports it, and a
// scenario's `animals` line is where that number is visible. Do not read
// `count: 1000` as a population.
//
// At frame 1,200 it is 167 organisms with 72 of 126 animals carrying food,
// which is the fed state the measurement needs; the organism count climbs
// from there as the plants seed.
//
// Not a bed anything should be concluded about biologically: it is crowded,
// fed by hand, and founded all at once.
(
    name: "crowded_bench",
    title: "CROWDED BENCH",
    question: "What does a breeding-rule lookup cost when one big colony lives among a lot of plants?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 1000),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 16),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 32),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 48),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 64),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 80),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 96),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 112),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 128),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 144),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 160),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 176),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 192),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 208),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 224),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 240),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 272),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 288),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 304),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 320),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 336),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 352),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 368),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 384),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 400),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 416),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 432),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 448),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 464),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 480),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 496),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 1200, every: 1200, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "windfall", x: 200, cells: 40)),
        (at: 1200, every: 1200, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "windfall", x: 312, cells: 40)),
    ],
    horizon: 30000,
)
